config APP_DFU
	bool "OTA / DFU image confirmation and upload hooks"
	default y
	depends on MCUMGR_GRP_IMG && BOOTLOADER_MCUBOOT
	help
	  Housekeeping around MCUboot image updates delivered over SMP: log the
	  running image version, confirm a freshly swapped-in image once it has
	  proven it can run, and quiesce Channel Sounding while an upload is in
	  flight. The manual slot commands come from Zephyr's MCUBOOT_SHELL.

if APP_DFU

config APP_DFU_CONFIRM_DELAY_S
	int "Self-confirm delay for a test image (seconds)"
	default 10
	range 0 300
	help
	  How long a newly swapped-in (unconfirmed) image must keep running
	  before it marks itself confirmed. A crash, fault or watchdog reset
	  before this deadline leaves the image unconfirmed, so MCUboot reverts
	  to the previous one on the next boot. Set to 0 to confirm immediately
	  (no revert protection).

config APP_DFU_PAUSE_CS
	bool "Stop Channel Sounding while an image upload is in progress"
	default y
	depends on APP_CS
	help
	  Writing the incoming image into RRAM stalls the CPU in bursts, which
	  disturbs Channel Sounding subevent timing. Stop ranging when an upload
	  starts; the device reboots into the new image when it completes.

endif # APP_DFU
